lly do  [Music]  from the moment she was born she began  using her feet for everyday tasks  and by the age of five she had her heart  set on something else that many people  thought was impossible  victoria told her mum she wanted to be a  dancer  [Music]  victoria has won competitions for a  dance school and she came second in a tv  town contest  [Music]  i think kids even with arms wouldn't be  able to do as much as you can do so what  made you want to get into dancing  especially having no arms okinawa physio  for you what didn't make me give up was  the people who were always by my side  who supported me in all my decisions  especially when i decided i wanted to  dance  my teachers welcomed me from my first  experimental class  which gave me strength  but also joy  cinco says  [Music]  yes  two years ago i made the decision to  have my leg removed  it was growing in the wrong direction  so having a prosthetic leg has helped me  do all the things i couldn't do before  but victoria's disability could have  stopped her from doing everyday tasks  never mind achieving her dreams  she just simply hasn't let it and that  is amazing  so  when you go into the shops  do people stare  yeah they will stare at you yeah seeing  our customers  how did you do that  wow  yeah wow  one you're one more right now  thank you thanks ciao ciao  [Music]  is that you  yeah  my brother my mom and my  sister is that is that a bruise bruise  on your nose it was saying  i always especially at that age i used  to tap my nose on my forehead because i  would fall  oh so when you when you fell it made a  mark on your nose because you didn't  have the hands yeah i've fallen a lot  getting used to my leg i fell on my  hands but i've had a lot of falls so  i kind of get i kind of get what you  mean  wow  we all love watching you dance but what  do you get out of dance  el  salvador i feel very strong connection  to my body when i'm dancing  whether it be ballet jazz tap  i'm completely in the moment as if  nothing else matters  but despite vittoria proving she can do  anything dancers with arms can do  professional ballet companies she would  love to perform with say they do not  recruit disabled dancers for their  productions  i found out that there are some  specialist companies for disabled  dancers  but vittorio doesn't want that  she believes she should have the same  opportunity as any other dancer she  wants to audition for the world's main  ballet companies  [Music]  for now victoria's only audience is on  social media her video posts are  followed by nearly half a million people  [Music]  i will teach you some steps yeah why not  [Music]  ah  [Music]  victoria gets recognized a lot  [Music]  among her army of instagram followers is  a world famous professional ballet  dancer brazilian thiago solas  he was a principal performer for the  world famous royal ballet company in  london  thiago saugas has invited victoria to a  private dance lesson at a school in rio  de janeiro  [Music]  what does it mean to you to have a world  famous ballet dancer reach out to you on  instagram how long will there be  throughout this whole journey with dance  god is always putting people in my path  to help me my family friends and  teachers people like thiego soros  [Applause]  [Music]  thiago is teaching vittorio dance he is  created just for her and they will  perform it to a piece of music that is  special to him  [Music]  [Music]  it's a dream come true for me to meet  diego sores i was nervous and it's a  tense day but it is also the realization  of my dreams  i don't think i've met anyone who would  have the courage to do that not be  scared about what people think sing  if i can get into college i can keep  dancing and learning  and then i can inspire other people by  performing across the world  if that happens it will prove that  ballet can be more  [Music]  inclusive as their day together is due  to come to an end thiago suddenly  announces a surprise for vit